nodejs.explanation:
**Node.js** lets you run JavaScript on the server. Combined with **Express.js** you can build powerful REST APIs.

**Why Node.js?**
• Same language (JavaScript) for frontend and backend
• Non-blocking I/O — handles many requests at once
• Huge NPM ecosystem — 2 million+ packages
• Used by Netflix, LinkedIn, PayPal, Uber

**Express.js Example — REST API:**
```javascript
const express = require('express');
const app = express();
app.use(express.json());

// GET all students
app.get('/students', (req, res) => {
  res.json([{ id:1, name:'Rehan' }, { id:2, name:'Ali' }]);
});

// POST add student
app.post('/students', (req, res) => {
  const { name } = req.body;
  res.json({ message: `Added ${name} successfully!` });
});

app.listen(3000, () => console.log('Server running on port 3000'));
```

**Key Concepts:**
• Middleware — runs between request and response
• JWT — JSON Web Tokens for authentication
• REST API — GET, POST, PUT, DELETE methods
• Environment Variables — .env files for secrets

💡 **Tip:** Learn Node.js + Express + MongoDB together — they form the MERN stack!

css.explanation:
**CSS (Cascading Style Sheets)** makes websites beautiful — it controls colors, fonts, layout, and animations.

**Selectors:**
• Element — `p { }`, `h1 { }`
• Class — `.card { }`, `.btn { }`
• ID — `#header { }`
• Pseudo — `a:hover { }`, `li:first-child { }`

**Box Model:**
• Content → Padding → Border → Margin

**Flexbox — 1D Layout:**
```css
.container {
  display: flex;
  justify-content: center;  /* horizontal */
  align-items: center;       /* vertical */
  gap: 16px;
}
```

**CSS Grid — 2D Layout:**
```css
.grid {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
  gap: 20px;
}
```

**Responsive Design:**
```css
@media (max-width: 768px) {
  .grid {
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
  }
}
```

**Animations:**
```css
.btn {
  transition: all 0.3s ease;
}
.btn:hover {
  transform: scale(1.05);
  background: #1D4ED8;
}
```

💡 **Tip:** Master Flexbox and Grid — they solve 90% of layout problems!

java.explanation:
**Java** is one of the most widely used programming languages — used in Android apps, enterprise software, and backend systems.

**4 Pillars of OOP:**
• **Encapsulation** — hiding data inside a class (private fields)
• **Inheritance** — child class inherits from parent class
• **Polymorphism** — same method, different behavior
• **Abstraction** — showing only essential details, hiding complexity

**Example — Inheritance & Polymorphism:**
```java
class Animal {
    void speak() {
        System.out.println("Animal speaks");
    }
}

class Dog extends Animal {
    @Override
    void speak() {
        System.out.println("Dog says: Woof! 🐕");
    }
}

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Animal a = new Dog();
        a.speak(); // Dog says: Woof!
    }
}
```

**Java Collections:**
• ArrayList — dynamic array
• LinkedList — doubly linked list
• HashMap — key-value pairs
• HashSet — unique elements
• TreeMap — sorted map

**Exception Handling:**
```java
try {
    int result = 10 / 0;
} catch (ArithmeticException e) {
    System.out.println("Error: " + e.getMessage());
} finally {
    System.out.println("Always runs");
}
```

💡 **Tip:** Java is great for placements — most IT companies use Java in backend interviews!
